{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966800,"nonce":"nfdlgyyNs5Oa1YXnUbsOqtHSRNI=","title":"Reactive\u003cbool\u003e props bound to an FSM ctx field silently fell back to LITERAL: the bool","message":"**Symptom.** `cn.Switch(checked = Play.busy)` / `cn.Checkbox(...)` neither\ntracked the FSM nor wrote back. Compiling proved nothing: a prop that lowers\nto LITERAL compiles perfectly and just snapshots the build-time value.\n\n**Cause (fixed 8949588a).** `Play.busy` resolves to\n`__signal_get_by_id_bool(\u003cid\u003e)`, which `lower_reactive_args` Shape A' knows.\nBut a bool reaching an integer-typed arg slot is wrapped in\n`if \u003cgetter\u003e { 1 } else { 0 }`, and neither Shape A (bare Variable) nor A'\n(wrapped getter) sees through it, so it fell to Shape C, LITERAL.\n\nBoth directions then broke at once, which is what made it look like two bugs:\nthe widget read a constant, AND `bridge::bool_state` mints a FRESH signal for\na literal, so the toggle wrote to a signal nothing else referenced.\n\n**Fix.** `unwrap_bool_int_coercion` strips the `If(cond, 1, 0)` shape, and all\nthree recognizers match against the stripped `probe` while the literal path\nstill encodes the original node. f64 props were unaffected, which is why\n`Progress(value = Play.pct)` worked and the toggles did not.\n\n**Testing this class of bug** (`crates/blinc_cn_dsl/tests/\ncn_toggle_binding.rs`): a compile-only test cannot see it. What is needed:\n\n- walk the builder tree for an element with a POINTER_UP handler and\n  `EventHandlers::dispatch` an `EventContext` -- that is a click, no renderer\n  required (`on_click` registers under POINTER_UP, there is no CLICK type)\n- install the notifier the host installs, `set_stateful_deps_notifier(|ids|\n  blinc_layout::check_stateful_deps(ids))`, or `Signal::set` notifies nobody\n  and the widget never refreshes\n- assert BOTH directions, and cover the FSM-ctx shape separately from the\n  plain-signal shape: the plain signal already worked while the ctx field did\n  not\n- `BlincDsl::{set,get}_signal_bool` exist for this (added with the fix); the\n  FSM ctx field is a normal signal named `__fsm_ctx_\u003cFsm\u003e_\u003cfield\u003e`\n\n**Debugging technique.** One `tracing::debug!` on the LITERAL fallback arm of\n`expand_reactive`, printing `inner_ty` and `arg.node`, named the exact AST\nshape in one run. There are no dump env vars in `blinc_dsl_core`.\n\nSee gotcha lower reactive args wrapped getter,\nproject cn reactive prop migration, gotcha dsl mixed type computed.","files":null}]}